      "width": 2048,
      "height": 1536,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "Public domain",
      "artist": "Sindre Skrede",
      "description": "The old gun emplacement at Fjell Festning (Fjell Fortress), as it appeared in mid 2004. The gun was the B-tower from the German battleship Gneisenau. The steel plating lying in front in the picture, is armour from the now removed gun turret. \n\nThe emplacement has later been modified, and a large glass housing has been placed on top of it. This was mainly to prevent rain entering the main tunnel system, but the building also contains a café. On the outside, the grass was removed (and the gunpost for a while looked as it did when the gun was operational), rain coating was applied, but dirt has now been put back on the concrete, a road (not original) has been constructed and a building containing toilets has been built close to the gun emplacement.",
      "dateCreated": "2004-06-04",
      "categories": [
        "Fjell Festning",
        "June 2004 Norway photographs",
        "PD-self",
        "Self-published work",
        "Taken with Canon Digital IXUS"
      ],
